       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day (prescription dosing). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. This much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum daily dose\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for pain, as a lower-dose option\n- **1600 mg total daily**, for example 400 mg four times daily, if the 1600 was meant as a daily total\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy before it's entered."
